{"agent":"bg79","data":{"by":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`clash_report` constructs strings with `p0!r` and `p1!r`, where `p0` and `p1` are globs (strings like `\"brief.py\"`). But in `ddflow/services/leases/claim.py` at line 271, the author writes: `named, _ids = clash_report(glob_clashes(state, cfg, it, holder, mine, now))` and then formats it as `f\"{item_id} writes {named}\"`. When a claim fails due to a glob clash, `clash_report` returns a string containing format parts like `'brief.py' overlaps 'brief.py' held by ...`. When combined with `claim.py`'s exception message, this prints `item_id writes 'brief.py' overlaps ...`, missing the expected introductory text or failing to correctly describe the overlapping files because `glob_clashes` unpacks `c.pair` where `c.pair` is `(mine_glob, theirs_glob)`. The function signature of `glob_clashes` returns `(c.item, c.lease, c.pair)`, but `_glob_clashes` in admission.py produces pairs from `conflicts(globs, lease.globs, shared)`, where the first element is from `mine` and the second from `theirs`. In `claim.py`, the old code was:\n`f\"{item_id} writes {pair[0]!r} which overlaps {pair[1]!r} held by {lease.holder} on {other_id}\"`.\nThe new `clash_report` omits the `item_id writes` and `which` and `on {oid}` in a way that produces malformed English grammar (`'brief.py' overlaps 'brief.py' held by H on I; 'other.py' overlaps ...`), and when interpolated into `f\"{item_id} writes {named}\"`, it duplicates the item prefix and loses the clarity of the single-clash message.","digest":"932bde85f5128b62","family":"google","location":"ddflow/services/leases/common.py:65","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/leases/common.py:65"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The rewritten `update --globs` refusal still does not name holders or queue places. `queued_ahead` may collect every overlapping waiter, but the text thrown away that list and hard-codes `queued behind earlier waiters ([lease].wait_queue)`. Given an update of `a.py` and `b.py` while Z is queued on `a.py` and W on `b.py`, the caller sees `those globs (…) are queued behind earlier waiters ([lease].wait_queue)`, with no holder and a literal field path instead of each glob’s waiter — the same one-conflict opacity B-glob-refusal-names-one-conflict asked to fix.","digest":"05d00ff13337aeb3","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/leases/lifecycle.py:198","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/leases/lifecycle.py:198"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":20027,"diff_sha":"e1ecaeb548c7959cd1b43ce42675336397f9f83f2a437e1d198e51f9eb078c7e","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-glob-refusal-names-one-conflict","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":63.0,"family":"google","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","output_digest":"9aaf1fa6c2e7c4de","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-glob-refusal-names-one-conflict.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T162459Z-3a49147f.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"634b3b7cd9f971c773658d2f4f93374505e398c5","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lifecycle/claim_guard_queued.py":"100644 9021ba1edd4eea54709a5aa9b9e6bebf82487096","ddflow/api/lifecycle/reservations.py":"100644 01443f0e90baf58e7bb3a5415c31e1bdae1ee8aa","ddflow/core/admission.py":"100644 f24abf988ee4fadba672c79718fadbe3fbfcb9be","ddflow/services/leases/__init__.py":"100644 bdc767b9f10890d13d2734b9b1837c7b5ccc375a","ddflow/services/leases/claim.py":"100644 00e542bbc8290e3094dd0c6c7a8ff39027af15f9","ddflow/services/leases/common.py":"100644 f6539fa15b5ba842f9d6fd6afdf0bed98d267d8a","ddflow/services/leases/lifecycle.py":"100644 9c0f885784f7eda77df626a84489039ab924a169","ddflow/services/waiting.py":"100644 8000871f012b7e87cbcd9ccd570f678890cf352